  "problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{90}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{0}^{∘}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The angles ${45}^{∘},$ ${90}^{∘}$ and ${0}^{∘}$ are special angles, and their trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{90}^{∘}=0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{0}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{90}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{0}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+0+1 & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+2}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
